# Playwright E2E

Location: `frontend/e2e/`, config: `frontend/playwright.config.ts`.

## Commands (run without asking)

```bash
pnpm test:e2e:frontend
pnpm --filter frontend test:e2e
```

## Conventions

- Specs: `*.spec.ts` under `e2e/`
- Prefer `getByRole` / `getByText` / `getByTestId` over CSS selectors
- Assert with web-first `expect(...).toBeVisible()`
- After client-side navigation use `expect(page).toHaveURL(...)` — not `page.waitForURL` (SPA may not fire `load`)
- Dashboard sidebar: **Users / Roles / Permissions** sit under **Access control** — use `e2e/helpers/dashboard-nav.ts`
- GDPR export JSON shape: `{ exportedAt, user: { email, … }, auditEvents }`; anonymize soft-deletes — assert toast + row gone, not `@anonymized.local` in grid
- `/dashboard/audit-logs` redirects to `/dashboard/site-settings?tab=audit`; viewer without site-settings/audit perms sees generic access denied (no `AUDIT_READ` label)
- `mfa.spec` must call `disableAdminMfa` in `finally` — enrollment persists on the shared admin user
- Keep tests independent; no shared mutable state
- After changing UI flows, update/add matching e2e specs and **run** them

## Cursor agent

When editing frontend pages/features or e2e specs: run related Playwright tests and fix failures before finishing.
